        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "body": "## Overview\n\nfzt is currently a monolith — engine, rendering, and CLI frontend in one binary. It's been successfully reused in three contexts (CLI/`at`, WASM/homepage, picker), but each reuse hits friction because the engine and frontend are coupled. This issue tracks the extraction into composable layers.\n\n## Architecture\n\n### fzt-core (Go package)\n\nThe engine. No rendering, no I/O. Pure state management and scoring.\n\n- Tree data structure (nodes, children, leaves)\n- Scope management (push, pop, breadcrumb state)\n- Fuzzy scoring and ranking\n- Cursor position and selection state\n- Search state and filtering\n- Query handling\n- Configuration: `--accept-nth`, `--search-depth=N`, etc.\n\nExposes a `TreeProvider` interface for pluggable data sources:\n\n```go\ntype TreeProvider interface {\n    LoadChildren(path string) []TreeNode\n}\n```\n\nImplementations:\n- **YAMLProvider**: loads full tree upfront from YAML (CLI, homepage bookmarks)\n- **DirProvider**: reads one directory on scope push (picker)\n\n### fzt-style (shared visual identity)\n\nThe \"look\" of fzt, consumed by all frontends:\n\n- Catppuccin Mocha palette values\n- DOS font configuration (PerfectDOSVGA437, Nerd Font icons)\n- CRT effect parameters (scanlines, vignette, rounded corners, cursor blink)\n- Spacing, border styles, element sizing\n\nTerminal frontend translates these into ANSI codes. Browser frontend translates them into CSS variables. One source of truth — change here, propagates everywhere.\n\n### Terminal frontend (current fzt CLI)\n\n- Imports fzt-core for state\n- Imports fzt-style for visual config\n- Renders ANSI output to terminal\n- Handles keyboard input\n- This is what `at`/automate and direct `fzt` invocation use\n\n### Browser frontend (replaces current WASM approach)\n\n- Imports fzt-core compiled to WASM (headless — no ANSI rendering)\n- Imports fzt-style as CSS variables\n- Renders DOM elements natively (no ANSI parsing layer)\n- Handles keyboard + mouse/click events\n- Used by homepage and any future browser-based fzt usage\n\nEliminates the current translation layer: Go renders ANSI -\u003e JS parses ANSI -\u003e JS creates styled spans. Instead: JS asks WASM core \"what's the state?\" -\u003e JS renders DOM directly.\n\n### Picker frontend\n\n- Imports fzt-core with DirProvider\n- Imports fzt-style for visual config\n- Renders via terminal (same as CLI frontend, or could share it)\n- Lazy loads directories on scope push\n- `--search-depth=1` restricts search to current scope level\n- Initial tree: drive roots, pre-expanded along focused_dir path\n- See nelsong6/fzt-picker#1 for picker-specific details\n\n## Coupling model\n\n| Layer | Shared via fzt-core | Shared via fzt-style | Per-frontend |\n|-------|-------------------|---------------------|-------------|\n| Tree state + scope | Yes | - | - |\n| Fuzzy scoring | Yes | - | - |\n| Cursor + selection | Yes | - | - |\n| Search + filtering | Yes | - | - |\n| Colors + palette | - | Yes | Override if needed |\n| Font + spacing | - | Yes | Override if needed |\n| CRT effects | - | Yes | Override if needed |\n| Rendering (ANSI/DOM) | - | - | Yes |\n| Input handling | - | - | Yes |\n| Click/hover support | - | - | Browser only |\n| Data source (YAML/dir) | - | - | Via TreeProvider |\n\n**Workflow**: \"Want this change in all frontends? Put it in fzt-core or fzt-style. Only in one? Put it in that frontend.\" The decision is explicit every time.\n\n## Motivation\n\n- Picker needs lazy loading — fundamentally incompatible with \"load everything upfront\"\n- Homepage WASM has an unnecessary ANSI translation layer\n- Terminal-only changes currently require WASM recompile + homepage redeploy\n- Nelson keeps finding new uses for fzt — the library makes each one cheaper\n- Visual identity stays locked via fzt-style while frontends iterate independently",
